Subject: [PATCH 19/19] ntdll: Add syscall wrappers to work around clang ABI
 breakage (from upstream f43402cde33).

Clang assumes callers zero-extend narrow integer arguments, which the PE side
(built with GCC) does not, so BOOLEAN syscall arguments can arrive with dirty
upper bits on a clang-built Unix side (any macOS build). Upstream fixed this in
wine-11.1 after moving the table to syscall.c; this places the same wrappers
around Proton's table in loader.c and undefines the redirects afterwards.
